        },
        {
          "id": 1074452669,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Wrong library HINT was used, \"bin\" instead of \"lib\", and utilize PATH_SUFFIXES helps in certain scenarios better I have found, at least in my weird system.\n\npkg-config fetches the first match and nothing more, this makes it impossible to control which version to utilize if multi version exist in the system",
          "author": {
            "id": 6524193,
            "username": "oakimk",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Joakim Karlsson",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/6524193/avatar.png?v=1789063004",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/oakimk"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-08-23T12:23:53.770Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-08-23T12:24:01.533Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 172845569,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 7866,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 1074938651,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "`GNUTLS_HINTS` is a Wireshark specific Windows thing, and I suspect `bin` is working as intended. Removing pkg-config makes `GNUTLS_INCLUDEDIR` and `GNUTLS_LIBDIR` useless.\n\nI don't follow your argument about pkg-config and multiple versions. The proper mechanisms for influencing the search using CMake should work fine. See the [relevant CMake manual page](https://cmake.org/cmake/help/latest/command/find_package.html#id7).\n\nI don't think using `PATH_SUFFIXES` is appropriate for `include` and `lib`.\n\nWould be helpful to know why your system is weird and what was the issue encountered.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2639362,
            "username": "jvalverde",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "João Valverde",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bea5f745397cf5a2fe0526df96ec143db47f9334340ab56515038832be57e976?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/jvalverde"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-08-23T17:49:24.167Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-08-23T17:49:24.167Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 172845569,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 7866,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 1078901244,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "For hints the path should be `lib` not `bin` since it's this folder you will find the .so files `gnutls libgnutls-28 libgnutls-30`.\n\nRegarding removal of pkg-config, there is a whole mix of use and and not use in the CMakes files, however what I found it's kinda of a legacy way of doing it.\n\nUsing PATH_SUFFIXES fixes same problem in other libs for me, see !7866 and !7518",
          "author": {
            "id": 6524193,
            "username": "oakimk",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Joakim Karlsson",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/6524193/avatar.png?v=1789063004",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/oakimk"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-08-26T06:55:09.433Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-08-26T06:55:09.433Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 172845569,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
